<main><div class="wrap"><article class="panel panel-pad markdown-page"><h1>Scientific Review, Focus-Site Audit &amp; PhD Analysis of <code>0.2778</code> (<code>2026-10-26</code>)</h1>
<h2>1. Executive Summary Across <code>KANLERGEMSDOE3</code>, All 9 Focus Sites &amp; Broader Portfolio</h2>
<p>We reviewed all <strong>9 focus repositories</strong> (<code>GEMSDOE24</code>, <code>GEMSDOE25</code>, <code>GEMSDOE27</code>, <code>GEMSDOE28</code>, <code>GEMSDOE30</code>, <code>GEMSDOE31</code>, <code>GEMSDOE32</code>, <code>GEMSDOE33</code>, <code>GEMSDOE36</code>) plus key non-family portfolio benchmarks (<code>19GEMSDOE</code>, <code>GEMSDOE63</code>, <code>GEMSDOE70</code>, <code>GEMSDOE76</code>, <code>GEMSDOE92</code>), restored the hash-pinned competition + public USGS/DOE external stack + <strong>417 downloadable/calibration rasters (<code>389</code> unique SHA-256 digests)</strong> autonomously via git smart HTTP, fixed shared template bugs (<code>IR-TEMPLATE-CODELOAD-01</code>, <code>IR-TEMPLATE-ROOT-DEPTH-03</code>), and executed our frozen 3-experiment geological lane <strong><code>KANLER-H1</code> (<code>DCAP-LHC</code>)</strong>.</p>
